Pilot management
It must be recalled that communication between Pilot and Master must be continuous. If Master has a doubt
regarding action taken by the pilot, he must immediately ask for explanation and confirm that he agrees. Pilot
must, when he is going to start an action, in normal transit or in emergency or abnormal situation as it is the case
here, explain briefly to Master what is his intention and ask for his agreement. Master must clearly state to pilot when he takes over the control. AIS is an additional source of navigational information. It does not replace, but supports, navigational systems
such as radar ARPA. ARPA should always be set on “Target priority” and not on “AIS priority”. All means available should be used for collision avoidance and, as far as possible, well in advanced. 4.

